          "title": "You'll want to know: zwar",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "zwar — \"admittedly (zwar … aber); to be precise (und zwar)\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Das Hotel ist zwar teuer, aber es liegt direkt am Strand. The hotel is expensive, admittedly, but it is right on the beach."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Zwar … aber grants one point and then turns; the verb stays second: das Hotel ist zwar teuer. Und zwar adds detail: heute, und zwar um acht."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "zwar is inherited from Middle High German ze wāre \"in truth, indeed\" (EtymDB), from ze \"to, in\" and wār \"true\": \"true, but …\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
